The default Singly Linked List is a struct with a pointer to a head, 
and a set of function pointers to do operations on the list members :

-get
-insert
-add


The standard list takes in
get(list, index)

to simply return a pointer to the desired contents



insert(list, index, contents, size) or add(list, contents, size)

to add an element to the list at a given position
with a pointer to contents

AUTO, IGNORE, and LITERAL are also supplied if the
user desires more granular control over memory
supplied to an allocation in a list

type_safe_singly_linked_list is a type safe version of
the list, which uses explicitly provided string literals
and stringized parameters from defines to provide type
checking at runtime.
